     Due to the number of people asking "I have Nethack but only a 64K comp-
uter?  Why does the game access the disk for five minutes ever move?" and
so forth, shouldn't the official distribution come with a file on memory
management?  i.e. Get ahold of DOS 3.1 if possible (less memory use, but
it won't handle high-density disks, I believe), load as few mem-res programs
as possible (I use 0, and put 4DOS in swapping mode so as to use only 3K
of memory, and end up with about 599,000 free.  Hopefully, I can get ahold
of DOS 3.1 and save another 15K or so, or whatever it is).  If you have more
than 640K, run a disk cache or ramdisk (disk cache is better, or if you have
a LOT of extra memory, just copy the executable into the ramdisk.)  If you
don't have 640K, you're out of luck.  
     I think that would help a lot of people.

